    [4522] = {
        achievementId = 4522,
        name = "Soul Power",
        category = "Dungeons",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Soul Power",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Keep four Corrupted Soul Fragments alive at Bronjahm's death using a prepared group or the specialized solo route.\n\n1. Enter the Forge of Souls on Heroic with a HUNTER for this solo route. Clear trash around Bronjahm, the FIRST boss. Put your pet on Passive and bind Move To, Disengage and a single-target finishing attack. Trailblazer, Pathfinding and Posthaste help with the return runs; remove uncontrolled damage effects.\n\n2. Start combat by moving the passive pet onto Bronjahm, without attacking yourself. Move the pet toward the entrance-side ramp and park it near 47.0, 53.1 on the Forge of Souls map, beside the chain near the ramp's top. The PET must hold aggro so Bronjahm casts Corrupt Soul on you.\n\n3. Stand on the open grate around 54.4, 57.5 with the boss in sight. When Corrupt Soul STARTS casting, Disengage backward onto the lower slanted grate around 56, 58. Land there BEFORE the cast finishes and stuns you. The fragment now has a longer route back to Bronjahm.\n\n4. Run back around to the casting position for the next cast, roughly thirty seconds later. Repeat until THREE fragments are alive. Keep yourself in casting range and line of sight between drops; missing a cycle lets the first fragment catch the boss.\n\n5. After the third drop, use your speed cooldown to return toward the pet. Use Move To repeatedly to pull Bronjahm BACK toward his boss room, away from the approaching first fragment. Remain in sight and at enough distance for the FOURTH fragment to spawn on you.\n\n6. As soon as FOUR fragments are alive, single-target Bronjahm to death before any reaches him. Do not cleave the fragments. If a fragment is consumed or the boss resets, rebuild the setup before killing him; the achievement needs four living fragments at the killing blow.",
