        mountCategory = "Dungeon and Raids",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare drop with daily or weekly loot limits can require many repeated clears.\n\n1. At the ground-level Icecrown Citadel raid entrance (53.7, 87.0 in Icecrown), set the legacy raid to 25-player Heroic. Enter the raid itself, not one of the nearby five-player dungeons. Use an unsaved weekly lockout.\n\n2. Clear Marrowgar and Deathwhisper, then start the gunship event. Take a rocket pack if needed, use the cannons, and handle the enemy mage if the cannons freeze. Continue through Deathbringer Saurfang.\n\n3. Clear all three upper branches needed to unlock the Frozen Throne: Festergut, Rotface and Putricide; the Blood Princes and Blood-Queen Lana'thel; then Sindragosa. Use the transporters as they unlock. For this mount-only route, you can pass around Valithria Dreamwalker without healing her.\n\n4. Make sure Putricide's and the other wing-end access requirements are finished, then use the central upper-spire teleporter to the Frozen Throne. Confirm that the Lich King encounter is still 25-player Heroic before telling Tirion to begin.\n\n5. Defeat the Lich King while avoiding Shadow Traps and the platform edge. At his scripted mass-kill ending, remain in the encounter and wait for the resurrection and Tirion's sequence; do not release spirit simply because he killed you. Finish him when attackable again.\n\n6. Loot the Lich King and use Invincible's Reins if they drop. This is a rare weekly chance, not a guaranteed Heroic reward. Return after reset or clear on other eligible characters; a Normal kill or 10-player kill is not a mount attempt.\n\n7. Learn the finished mount, then check Invincible's Reins in your achievement list. A drop attempt or riding another player's mount does not complete this collection criterion.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4625",
        difficultyReason = "A rare drop with daily or weekly loot limits can require many repeated clears.",
        difficulty = "hard",
        achievementId = 4625,
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4625#comments",
    },
    [4626] = {
        category = "Mounts",
        source = "And I'll Form the Head!",
        npcId = 33288,
        tips = "Current Ulduar has one merged size. The mount condition is zero assisting Keepers, not a 25-player selector. Do not talk to the defeated Keepers to request their help.",
        sourceComments = { 806970, 2019134 },
        waypoints = {
            {
                mapID = 120,
                x = 0.41600000000000004,
                y = 0.182,
                step = 1,
                label = "Ulduar raid entrance - zero-Keeper Yogg route",
                mapName = "The Storm Peaks",
            },
        },
        itemId = 45693,
        name = "And I'll Form the Head!",
        mountCategory = "Dungeon and Raids",
        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare drop with daily or weekly loot limits can require many repeated clears.\n\n1. Enter the normal legacy Ulduar raid in the Storm Peaks (41.6, 18.2), rather than a queued Timewalking instance. Use your own weekly lockout. The old instructions to clear in 10-player and switch to 25-player are obsolete after Ulduar's merger.\n\n2. Start the entrance assault, use a siege vehicle if needed, and defeat Flame Leviathan. Continue through XT-002 Deconstructor and Kologarn into the inner ring. Ignis, Razorscale, and the Assembly of Iron are not required detours just to reach Yogg-Saron.\n\n3. Defeat Hodir, Thorim, Freya, and Mimiron to unlock the way onward. After each win, leave that Keeper's assistance dialogue alone. Their defeated friendly versions on the inner ring must not be asked to help in Yogg-Saron's chamber.\n\n4. Defeat General Vezax and enter Yogg-Saron's prison. Keep zero Keepers assisting. In the first phase, kill the spawned Guardians beside Sara so their explosions trigger the phase transition; repeatedly hitting Sara directly does not replace this mechanic.\n\n5. When the portal phase begins, enter a brain portal, clear the illusion's tentacles, and damage the brain before Induce Madness completes. Use the exit portal in time and avoid losing all Sanity; repeat the portal sequence if needed.\n\n6. In the final phase, turn away from Lunatic Gaze when necessary, kill Yogg-Saron, and loot him. Learn Mimiron's Head if it drops. Alone in the Darkness can confirm the zero-Keeper setup, but completing it does not guarantee the mount.\n\n7. Return after the weekly reset or use another eligible character if the mount did not drop. Re-running the same saved boss or changing a legacy size setting does not produce another roll.\n\n8. Learn the finished mount, then check And I'll Form the Head! in your achievement list. A drop attempt or riding another player's mount does not complete this collection criterion.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4626",
        difficultyReason = "A rare drop with daily or weekly loot limits can require many repeated clears.",
        difficulty = "hard",
        achievementId = 4626,
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4626#comments",
    },
    [4628] = {
        achievementId = 4628,
        name = "Heroic: Storming the Citadel (10 player)",
        category = "Raids",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Heroic: Storming the Citadel (10 player)",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - Defeat the required legacy raid bosses in the correct size and mode, allowing scripted events to finish.\n\n1. Outside Icecrown Citadel, set Legacy Raid Size to 10 players and Raid Difficulty to HEROIC. Enter the RAID portal at 53.5, 85.5 in Icecrown; the higher Frozen Halls dungeon entrance is different.\n\n2. Defeat Marrowgar and Deathwhisper, then take the elevator to the ramparts. Obtain and equip the faction ship's Goblin Rocket Pack, speak to the commander and start the Gunship Battle. Use a cannon as soon as the enemy ship arrives; build heat with Cannon Blast and spend it with Incinerating Blast.\n\n3. If the cannons freeze, jump across using the Rocket Pack, kill the battle-mage and jump back to your own ship. Resume cannon fire until victory. Cross to Saurfang's platform, speak to the commander and defeat Deathbringer Saurfang. Check all FOUR criteria before teleporting upstairs.",
